<title>LATVIA: FINANCE MINISTRY SIGNS AGREEMENT WITH EIB.</title>
<headline>FINANCE MINISTRY SIGNS AGREEMENT WITH EIB.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Latvian finance ministry said on Thursday it signed an agreement with the European Investment Bank (EIB) to allow it to start operations in the Baltic state.</p>
<p>The finance ministry said in a statement that the agreement set out the EIB's statutes in Latvia. A finance ministry spokesman said the status of the bank would be similar to that of the World Bank and other international organisations.</p>
<p>The two sides also discussed a state guarantee for an EIB loan worth 20 million Ecu to Ventspils port, the largest in the Baltic states.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
